new ModuleFederationPlugin({
  name: 'host',
  remotes: {
    profile: 'profile@https://cdn.example.com/profile/remoteEntry.js'
  },
  shared: {
    react: { singleton: true, requiredVersion: '^19.0.0' },
    'react-dom': { singleton: true, requiredVersion: '^19.0.0' },
    // exports AuthContext + useAuth()
    '@acme/auth': { requiredVersion: '^2.3.0' }
  }
});

referenceAnswer:
A React context is identified by the object returned from createContext, which is per module instance. Without singleton: true the shared scope is allowed to serve two copies of @acme/auth: the host renders the provider from its copy while the remote's useAuth() subscribes to the context object from the other copy, finds no matching provider above it, and falls back to the default passed to createContext. Any module that carries identity — react, react-dom, a router, a context or provider package, a global store — must be declared singleton:

```js
shared: {
  '@acme/auth': { singleton: true, requiredVersion: '^2.3.0' }
}
```

Keep the version aligned across the estate as well, since singleton resolution silently loads the higher version and only warns the lower-version consumer.

